<title>JAPAN: Queensland Treasury Corp launches dual samurai.</title>
<headline>Queensland Treasury Corp launches dual samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/Australian dollar dual currency samurai bond issue was announced by lead-manager Nikko Securities on Wednesday:</p>
<p>BORROWER Queensland Treasury Corp</p>
<p> AMT		 20 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    3.6 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  9 Dec 1999</p>
<p> TYPE		dual samurai</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  Dec 9</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	Nov 25-Dec 6</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     AA (S&amp;P), Aa2 (Moody's)</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nikko Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Sanwa Bank</p>
<p>NOTES: The currency to be used for redemption will be decided on November 9, 1999. If the Australian dollar is at or above 79.90 yen on that date, holders of the bonds will receive 500,000 yen for each 500,000-yen bond held at maturity. If the Australian dollar is at less than 79.90 yen on that date, holders of the bonds will receive 6,257.82 Australian dollars for each 500,000-yen bond held at maturity. ---Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-5473-3748</p>
</text>
